WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.463
You built central private D N S,
with zone groups placed by policy.

3
00:00:05.463 --> 00:00:08.541
You proved the vault resolves
to a private address

4
00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:11.838
inside the network and
refuses requests from outside.

5
00:00:11.838 --> 00:00:17.313
You checked its role-based access, purge
protection, firewall and rotation policy.

6
00:00:17.313 --> 00:00:20.912
And you found an allowed and a
denied read in its audit log.

7
00:00:20.912 --> 00:00:24.959
The evidence an I S S O keeps from
this module: the zones, links,

8
00:00:24.959 --> 00:00:30.657
endpoints and zone groups; policy compliance
for the private D N S and public-access

9
00:00:30.657 --> 00:00:35.033
policies; the two lookup results
and the refused public request;

10
00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:40.318
the vault properties, role assignments
at vault scope and rotation policies;

11
00:00:40.318 --> 00:00:43.951
the audit event rows; and the
restore test when it runs.

12
00:00:43.951 --> 00:00:46.963
Next is Module 5: policy,
drift and evidence,

13
00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:51.670
holding all of it in place and
handing the assessor what they need.
